# battement -- three intervals, six oscillators, no triggers at all.
#
# The Radigue lens: the music is the beating between near-unisons. Each pair
# is detuned so its difference frequency is a chosen tempo, and one very slow
# LFO nudges a single detune so the beat rate itself breathes.
#
#   octave pair   55 Hz    ~0.09 Hz beat -- an 11-second swell
#   root pair    110 Hz    ~0.21 Hz beat -- a 5-second pulse
#   fifth pair   165 Hz    ~0.34 Hz beat -- a 3-second flutter
#
# Nothing here is clocked. Nothing is struck. Render 8-12 minutes; the only
# events are the ones your ear invents. Fade in post.
#
# Companion to .claude/skills/ratsnest-inspiration (artist-lenses: Radigue).

# ---- the octave: slowest beat, carries the weight ----
o1 = vco { freq: 55hz, wave: tri }
o2 = vco { freq: 55hz, wave: tri }
0.00236 -> o2.v_oct

# ---- the root ----
r1 = vco { freq: 110hz, wave: tri }
r2 = vco { freq: 110hz, wave: tri }
0.00276 -> r2.v_oct

# ---- the just fifth (3/2) ----
f1 = vco { freq: 110hz, wave: tri }
f2 = vco { freq: 110hz, wave: tri }
0.58496 -> f1.v_oct
0.58496 -> f2.v_oct
0.00298 -> f2.v_oct

# ---- the hair the potentiometer moves by ----
# 24 minutes. The root pair's beat rate wanders between roughly 0.15 and
# 0.27 Hz, so the five-second pulse is never quite five seconds.
hair = lfo { wave: sine, freq: 0.0007hz }
hair -> r2.v_oct : 0.0008

# ---- one gentle filter, opening across nine minutes ----
bed = svf { cutoff: 240, res: 0.08 }
o1 -> bed.in : 0.22
o2 -> bed.in : 0.22
r1 -> bed.in : 0.15
r2 -> bed.in : 0.15
f1 -> bed.in : 0.09
f2 -> bed.in : 0.09

dawn = lfo { wave: tri, freq: 0.0018hz }
dawn -> bed.cutoff : 620

# ---- a room, not an effect ----
hall = reverb { decay: 0.9, damp: 0.28, mix: 1, predelay: 0.04,
                bandwidth: 0.93, mod_rate: 0.21, mod_depth: 16 }
bed.lp -> hall.in_l : 0.5
bed.lp -> hall.in_r : 0.5

m = mix { levels: [0.7, 0.55, 0.55], pans: [0, -0.85, 0.85] }
bed.lp -> m.in1
hall.out_l -> m.in2
hall.out_r -> m.in3

dc = dcblock { cutoff: 10hz }
m.out_l -> dc.in_l
m.out_r -> dc.in_r
dc.out_l -> out.left
dc.out_r -> out.right
-0.65 -> out.level

# The discipline: if this is boring, the modulation is too fast, not too
# small. Halve `hair`'s frequency before you add anything.
#
# Try next:
#   * retune the fifth to 0.58333 (tempered) and hear the stillness leave
#   * remove the fifth pair entirely for the first four minutes
#   * replace one tri with a `sine` -- the beat survives, the body goes
#   * add a third interval at 0.80735 (7/4) and take the fifth out
